# Editing this capsule

The server reads .gmi files directly off disk -- no rebuild required
after editing. Three ways to change what this capsule serves:

## 1. Built-in source editor (recommended)

Sign in to your Cloud in a Bottle compute space. Visit this capsule's
hostname over HTTPS and add /edit to the URL.

You'll get a sidebar with all .gmi files and a plain gemtext source
editor. Hit Save and agate serves the new content on the next request.

The editor lives at the HTTP side of this app (not the Gemini side),
behind the Cloud in a Bottle session, so only the compute-space owner
can use it.

## 2. Filestash

Open the Filestash app and navigate to app_data/gemini/content. The
.gmi files there are the pages you see here. Edit, save, and refresh
your Gemini client.

## 3. bottle app ssh (power user)

You can edit files directly from the shell using the Cloud in a Bottle CLI:

```
bottle app ssh gemini -- sh -c 'cat > /data/app_data/gemini/content/index.gmi'
```

(Paste your new content, Ctrl-D.)

